From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:31:31 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 13/28] Plutonium: pair from a browser over the addresses the
 server reports

T3's pairing QR lists only the desktop app's endpoints, so a browser on
loopback (the Plutonium shell) had none and showed no QR code. Without a
desktop bridge, Settings, Connections now uses ServerConfig.directEndpoints:
the server's LAN and tailnet addresses, and its Tailscale Serve name once it
answers. A loopback server with Tailscale Serve says so instead of "only this
machine can connect".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
